  "summary": "This slice finishes the chapter on configuring Vim per project: ALE linters and ‘textwidth’ are driven from .projections.json metadata via Projectionist queries and a User ProjectionistActivate autocommand, with notes on projection specificity, generic keys, local vimrc risks, and built-in projection keys. It then opens Appendix 1, which surveys future directions for Vim 8 and Neovim (LSP, :terminal, externalized tab bar/pop-up menu/status line GUIs, and embedding Neovim in Sublime Text and VSCode), and closes with footnotes, the bibliography, and back matter.",
